# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy CVE Suppressions for field-management-service
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These CVE IDs are scoped here (not in the repo-wide .trivyignore) so that
# the exemptions apply ONLY when scanning this service's container image.
# See .github/workflows/security.yml for how per-service ignore files are
# merged with the repo-wide .trivyignore at scan time.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-03-29
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# minimatch ReDoS / path-traversal (CVE-2026-26996, CVE-2026-27903, CVE-2026-27904)
# Package: minimatch 9.0.5 and 10.1.1 bundled inside npm@11.7.0's own
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/minimatch (npm-internal tooling).
# These are NOT part of the application's runtime dependency tree; they are
# only reachable when npm/npx itself processes packages (e.g., during the
# Prisma migration step on container startup).
# Accepted risk: npm's internal modules are not exposed to untrusted input
# at application runtime.
# Revisit: remove once npm ships a release bundling minimatch>=10.2.3.
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# tar path-traversal / symlink / permission-modification chain
# (CVE-2026-23745, CVE-2026-23950, CVE-2026-24842, CVE-2026-26960,
#  CVE-2026-29786, CVE-2026-31802)
# Package: tar 7.5.2 bundled inside npm@11.7.0's own
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/tar (npm-internal tooling).
# Note: tar does not currently appear in the repo root or this service's
# package-lock.json as an application dependency, and npm's bundled tar is
# not affected by package.json "overrides". This ignore is an accepted-risk
# exception for npm-internal tooling CVEs only.
# Revisit: remove once npm ships a release bundling tar>=7.5.11.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802

# tar <6.2.1 — arbitrary file creation via insufficient symlink checks
CVE-2024-28863

# tar <6.2.1 — denial of service via crafted tar archive headers
CVE-2024-28176

# @isaacs/brace-expansion@5.0.0 — DoS via unbounded brace range expansion
# Bundled inside npm@11.7.0 at /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/
# Not part of application runtime dependencies. Fixed in 5.0.1.
# Revisit: remove once npm ships a release bundling @isaacs/brace-expansion>=5.0.1.
CVE-2026-25547
